[
  {
    "uid": "C1017",
    "text": "The name on the bone does not establish whose bone it is",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4612,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "fragment-unverified",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4816,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-fragment-unverified",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1018",
    "text": "The fragment's label is not enough to establish whose bone it is. The honest result is uncertainty, not an authenticated relic.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4613,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "fragment-unverified",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4815,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-fragment-unverified",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1019",
    "text": "Trent: saints with Christ pray for people on earth",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4614,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-saints-pray",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1020",
    "text": "Trent teaches that saints with Christ continue to pray for people on Earth. The council therefore recommends asking for their help.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4615,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-saints-pray",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1021",
    "text": "Trent: Christ alone saves; saints are not other saviours",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4616,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-christ-alone",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1022",
    "text": "The council does not present saints as competing saviours. It nevertheless disagrees with Calvin about the legitimacy of requesting their aid.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4617,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-christ-alone",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1023",
    "text": "Trent: honour the person shown in the picture, not the paint",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4618,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-image-honour",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1024",
    "text": "The council denies that divinity or power resides in an image as such. It gives images a role in remembrance, instruction and honour directed to their subjects.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4619,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-image-honour",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1025",
    "text": "Trent: saints\u2019 bodies deserve honour because they belong to Christ",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4620,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-body-honour",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1026",
    "text": "The decree treats holy bodies as connected with Christ and with resurrection. This is a reason within its teaching, not an automatic identification of any labelled fragment.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4621,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-body-honour",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1027",
    "text": "Trent: newly claimed relics need examination and a bishop\u2019s approval",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4622,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-new-relic",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1028",
    "text": "The decree restricts recognition of new relics and approval of unusual images. A permissible category is not a licence for every particular object.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4623,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-new-relic",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1029",
    "text": "Case update: a record of who has kept this bone",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4624,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "new-record",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1030",
    "text": "A new record identifies some of the people who kept the bone. It strengthens the investigation, but gaps in its history remain and a bishop has not recognized it as a relic.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4625,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "new-record",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1031",
    "text": "Trent: ask saints to pray through Christ, not to replace him",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4626,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "saints-not-saviours",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1032",
    "text": "Trent says saints with Christ pray for people on earth. Asking for their prayers therefore means asking for help through Christ, not replacing him. Calvin still rejects the practice because he finds no biblical permission for it and thinks it obscures Christ's unique role.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4627,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "saints-not-saviours",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1033",
    "text": "Trent: saints pray through Christ. Calvin: no biblical permission; Christ is sidelined",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4628,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "prayer-disagreement",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4818,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-prayer-disagreement",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1034",
    "text": "Trent says saints pray through Christ rather than replacing him. Calvin rejects asking them, arguing that it lacks biblical permission and obscures Christ's unique role. They disagree about whether people should make these requests, not simply about what to call the saints.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4629,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "prayer-disagreement",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4817,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-prayer-disagreement",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1035",
    "text": "Trent allows honour directed through the painting to Stephen",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4630,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "panel-possible",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1036",
    "text": "Trent allows honour to pass through a painting to the person shown. The proposed Stephen painting fits that kind of use; the paint itself is not treated as divine.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4631,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "panel-possible",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1037",
    "text": "Trent permits this honour through a picture; Calvin rejects it",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4632,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "panel-still-disputed",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4820,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-panel-still-disputed",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1038",
    "text": "Trent says honour can pass through the picture to Stephen. Calvin rejects that devotional use. Both have now considered the same proposed painting.\n\nRedirecting the honour away from the paint explains Trent\u2019s position; it does not make Calvin accept it.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4633,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "panel-still-disputed",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4819,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-panel-still-disputed",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1039",
    "text": "Honouring saints\u2019 bones requires knowing this bone is a saint\u2019s",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4634,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "honour-needs-identity",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1040",
    "text": "A reason to honour genuine relics does not establish that this fragment is genuine. The object's identity still needs evidence.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4635,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "honour-needs-identity",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1041",
    "text": "This bone still needs examination and a bishop\u2019s recognition",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4636,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "recognition-pending",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1042",
    "text": "The claim about this bone still needs examination and a bishop's recognition. A name on its label and a partial history are not enough.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4637,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "recognition-pending",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1043",
    "text": "A record of the bone\u2019s past helps; it is not a bishop\u2019s approval",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4638,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "record-not-ruling",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1044",
    "text": "The new record helps trace who kept the bone. It does not verify every link in its history or amount to a bishop's approval.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4639,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "record-not-ruling",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1045",
    "text": "A better history for the bone would not remove Calvin\u2019s objection",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4640,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "evidence-not-consensus",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4822,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-evidence-not-consensus",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1046",
    "text": "A better history could support the bone's claimed identity, but Calvin would still reject religious honour to it. Whose bone it is and whether it should be venerated are different questions.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4641,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "evidence-not-consensus",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1047",
    "text": "Case: one infant ill, one well; neither chose wrong",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4642,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "two-infants",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1048",
    "text": "One infant is ill and the other is well. Neither has chosen a wrongful act. Does either child's health determine a need for forgiveness?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4643,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "two-infants",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1049",
    "text": "The sick infant has not chosen wrong; neither has the healthy infant",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4644,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "health-not-moral-test",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1050",
    "text": "Neither infant has chosen a wrong act. Illness in one child is not evidence that the child deliberately did wrong.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4645,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "health-not-moral-test",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1051",
    "text": "Luther: the pope can lift church penalties, not control God\u2019s mercy",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4646,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "papal-penalty-limit",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1052",
    "text": "In 1517 Luther limits the pope's own power to penalties imposed by church authority. He distinguishes declaring God's forgiveness from controlling it. The limits he proposes are disputed.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4647,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "papal-penalty-limit",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1053",
    "text": "Luther: an indulgence letter cannot command God to free a dead soul",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4648,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "letter-limited",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1054",
    "text": "An indulgence concerns penalties remaining after forgiveness. Luther further limits church authority: a papal letter cannot by its own power command God to release a dead soul.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4649,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "letter-limited",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1055",
    "text": "Luther: Christ\u2019s body comes with bread. Zwingli: bread points to the body",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4650,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "luther-zwingli-contrast",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1056",
    "text": "These two accounts differ about bodily presence. That does not yet locate Aquinas: his earlier changed-bread account is a third position to compare.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4651,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "luther-zwingli-contrast",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1057",
    "text": "Even if it is Stephen\u2019s bone, Calvin still rejects honouring it",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4652,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "authenticity-not-permission",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1058",
    "text": "The bone's identity remains unresolved, but Calvin's objection to honouring it does not depend on that uncertainty. A genuine object can still be disputed as a religious practice.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4653,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "authenticity-not-permission",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1059",
    "text": "The record helps trace the bone; it does not yet prove its identity",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4654,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "record-adds-evidence",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1060",
    "text": "The record adds evidence about the fragment's past. Its incomplete history does not yet establish the bone's identity or supply a bishop's approval.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4655,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "record-adds-evidence",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
